  "summary_en": "Bahrain's 2017 Cloud First Policy requires government entities to use cloud services for new or replacement ICT unless an alternative is justified. It sets security, data classification, backup and data residency principles, and assigns roles to SCICT, ICTGC and iGA. It has no AI or robotics content.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Government entities must use cloud services for new or replaced ICT unless an alternative is more cost-effective with equal security",
   "Cloud providers must meet international standards such as ISO 27001, SOC 1/2, PCI DSS and CSA",
   "Data classification drives security controls; agencies need backup in a second location across two regions",
   "Data residency restrictions are discouraged; open data is encouraged",
   "SCICT approves, ICTGC audits and oversees, and iGA acts as interface with providers"
  ],
